{"id": "eval-000036", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "circle", "answer": "49\\pi", "pred": "49\\pi", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the area of a circle, use the formula:\n\n$$\nA = \\pi r^2\n$$\n\nGiven that the radius $ r = 7 $ mm, substitute into the formula:\n\n$$\nA = \\pi (7)^2 = \\pi \\times 49\n$$\n\nSo, the area is:\n\n$$\n49\\pi \\text{ mm}^2\n$$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{49\\pi}$"}
{"id": "eval-000037", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "column_op", "answer": "667", "pred": "667", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To solve the subtraction problem:\n\n4294 - 3627\n\nStep 1: Start from the rightmost digit (units place).\n- 4 - 7: Since 4 is less than 7, we need to borrow 1 from the tens place.\n- 14 - 7 = 7\n\nStep 2: Move to the tens place.\n- After borrowing, the tens place is 9 (since 294 becomes 294 - 1 = 293, but we're borrowing from the tens place).\n- 9 - 2 = 7\n\nStep 3: Move to the hundreds place.\n- 2 - 6: Since 2 is less than 6, we borrow from the thousands place.\n- 12 - 6 = 6\n\nStep 4: Move to the thousands place.\n- 4 - 3 = 1\n\nNow, putting it all together:\n\n4294 - 3627 = 667\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{667}"}
