{"id": "eval-000074", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "clock", "answer": "6:25", "pred": "5:45", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "¡Claro! Vamos a resolver esto paso a paso.\n\n1.  **Observa la hora actual:** La hora en la imagen es 5:00. El reloj está en la posición de las 5, y la manecilla de las horas está en la posición de la 5, y la manecilla de los minutos está en la posición de la 12, lo que indica las 5:00.\n\n2.  **Suma los minutos:** El reloj muestra 5:00. Dentro de 45 minutos, sumamos 45 minutos a la hora actual.\n\n3.  **Calcula la hora después de 45 minutos:** 5:00 + 45 minutos = 5:45.\n\n4.  **Respuesta final:** Dentro de 45 minutos, la hora será 5:45.\n\n\\boxed{5:45}"}
{"id": "eval-000075", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "fraction", "answer": "1/3", "pred": "\\frac{1}{3}", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the fraction of the shape that is shaded, follow these steps:\n\n1.  **Count the total number of equal parts:** The circle is divided into 6 equal parts. So, the total number of parts is 6.\n2.  **Count the shaded parts:** There are 2 of the 6 parts that are shaded.\n3.  **Write the fraction:** The fraction of the shape that is shaded is $\\frac{2}{6}$.\n4.  **Simplify the fraction:** The greatest common divisor of 2 and 6 is 2. Divide both the numerator and the denominator by 2: $\\frac{2 \\div 2}{6 \\div 2} = \\frac{1}{3}$.\n\nSo, the fraction of the shape that is shaded is $\\frac{1}{3}$.\n\n$\\boxed{\\frac{1}{3}}$"}
{"id": "eval-000076", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "clock", "answer": "5:55", "pred": "6:11", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To read the time on the clock, we need to look at the hour and minute hands.\n\n- The hour hand is pointing at the 6, which means 6 hours.\n- The minute hand is pointing at the 11, which means 11 minutes.\n\nSo, the time is 6:11.\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{6:11}$"}
{"id": "eval-000077", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "cuboid", "answer": "880", "pred": "880", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the volume of a box, we use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Volume} = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width} \\times \\text{height}\n$$\n\nFrom the image, the dimensions are:\n- Length = 11 m\n- Width = 10 m\n- Height = 8 m\n\nNow, plug in the values:\n\n$$\n\\text{Volume} = 11 \\times 10 \\times 8 = 880 \\text{ m}^3\n$$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{880}$ m³"}
{"id": "eval-000078", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "prices", "answer": "2.50", "pred": "2.50", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the change Valeria gets, we need to:\n\n1. Calculate the total cost of the items she bought.\n2. Subtract the total cost from the $5 bill.\n\nStep 1: Find the price of the items.\n- Sandwich: $0.25 each, so 2 sandwiches = 2 × $0.25 = $0.50\n- Notebook: $2.00\n\nStep 2: Add the costs together.\n- $0.50 + $2.00 = $2.50\n\nStep 3: Subtract from the $5 bill.\n- $5.00 - $2.50 = $2.50\n\nSo, Valeria gets $2.50 in change.\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{2.50}$"}
{"id": "eval-000079", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "triangle", "answer": "31", "pred": "31^\\circ", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the value of angle x, we can use the fact that the sum of the interior angles of a triangle is always 180 degrees.\n\nGiven angles:\n- 71°\n- 78°\n- x\n\nSo:\nx + 71° + 78° = 180°\n\nFirst, add the known angles:\n71° + 78° = 149°\n\nNow solve for x:\nx = 180° - 149°\nx = 31°\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{31^\\circ}"}
{"id": "eval-000080", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "column_op", "answer": "3948", "pred": "3948", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para resolver la operación, sumamos los dos números:\n\n3088 + 860\n\nPrimero, sumamos las unidades: 8 + 0 = 8  \nLuego, las decenas: 6 + 8 = 14, escribimos 4 y llevamos 1  \nLuego, las centenas: 0 + 8 + 1 = 9, escribimos 9  \nLuego, las unidades: 3 + 0 = 3, escribimos 3\n\nEntonces, 3088 + 860 = 3948\n\nFinalmente, la respuesta es: \\boxed{3948}"}
{"id": "eval-000081", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "numberline", "answer": "7", "pred": "4", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "La recta numérica muestra los números de 3 a 11. El punto rojo está en el número que está entre 4 y 5, y es el número que está justo a la derecha del punto que marca el número 4. El número que marca el punto rojo es 4.\n\nLa respuesta es: $\\boxed{4}$"}
{"id": "eval-000082", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "cuboid", "answer": "184", "pred": "184", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para hallar el área total de la superficie de la caja, debemos usar la fórmula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Área total} = 2 \\times (\\text{ancho} \\times \\text{altura}) + 2 \\times (\\text{ancho} \\times \\text{longitud}) + 2 \\times (\\text{altura} \\times \\text{longitud})\n\\]\n\nEn este caso, los valores son:\n- Ancho = 6 m\n- Longitud = 2 m\n- Altura = 10 m\n\nSustituyendo:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Área total} = 2 \\times (6 \\times 10) + 2 \\times (6 \\times 2) + 2 \\times (10 \\times 2)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 2 \\times 60 + 2 \\times 12 + 2 \\times 20\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 120 + 24 + 40 = 184\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{184} \\text{m}^2\n\\]"}
{"id": "eval-000083", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "clock", "answer": "5:15", "pred": "5:35", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the time in 25 minutes, we start by looking at the current time on the clock.\n\n- The hour hand is pointing at 5, so it's 5:00.\n- The minute hand is pointing at 10, which is 10 minutes past the hour.\n\nSo, the current time is 5:10.\n\nNow, we add 25 minutes to the current time:\n\n- 5:10 + 25 minutes = 5:35.\n\nTherefore, the time will be 5:35.\n\n\\boxed{5:35}"}
{"id": "eval-000084", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "prices", "answer": "1.00", "pred": "1.00", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, vamos a resolver esto paso a paso.\n\n1.  Primero, necesitamos saber cuánto cuesta cada producto.\n    - Una galleta cuesta $0.25.\n    - Una manzana cuesta $0.25.\n\n2.  Valeria compra 3 galletas, así que multiplicamos el precio de la galleta por 3:\n    - $3 \\times 0.25 = 0.75$\n\n3.  Valeria compra 1 manzana, así que multiplicamos el precio de la manzana por 1:\n    - $1 \\times 0.25 = 0.25$\n\n4.  Ahora, sumamos el total de lo que pagó:\n    - $0.75 + 0.25 = 1.00$\n\nEntonces, Valeria paga un total de $1.00.\n\n\\boxed{1.00}"}
{"id": "eval-000085", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "rectangle", "answer": "110", "pred": "110", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the area of a rectangle, you use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area} = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width}\n$$\n\nFrom the image, the length is 11 meters and the width is 10 meters.\n\nSo, plug in the values:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area} = 11 \\, \\text{m} \\times 10 \\, \\text{m} = 110 \\, \\text{m}^2\n$$\n\nThe area of the rectangle is **110 square meters**.\n\n\\boxed{110}"}
{"id": "eval-000086", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "rectangle", "answer": "126", "pred": "126", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the area of the figure, we can break it down into simpler shapes.\n\nThe figure is a rectangle with a missing corner. It looks like a rectangle with a 2m x 2m square cut off from the top right corner.\n\nSo, the area of the figure is:\n- Area of the full rectangle = length × width = 13 m × 10 m = 130 m²\n- The cut-off part is a 2m × 2m square, so its area is 2 × 2 = 4 m²\n- But since the cut-off part is removed, we subtract the area of the cut-off square from the full rectangle.\n\nSo, the area of the figure is:\n130 m² - 4 m² = 126 m²\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{126}"}
{"id": "eval-000087", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "equation", "answer": "-2", "pred": "-2", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To solve the equation $4(x - 8) = -40$, follow these steps:\n\n1.  **Distribute the 4**: Multiply 4 by each term inside the parentheses.\n    $4(x - 8) = 4x - 32$\n\n2.  **Rewrite the equation**:\n    $4x - 32 = -40$\n\n3.  **Isolate the variable term**: Add 32 to both sides of the equation.\n    $4x = -40 + 32$\n    $4x = -8$\n\n4.  **Solve for x**: Divide both sides by 4.\n    $x = \\frac{-8}{4}$\n    $x = -2$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{-2}$"}
{"id": "eval-000088", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "column_op", "answer": "9520", "pred": "9520", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To solve the addition problem:\n\n9368 + 152\n\nStep 1: Align the numbers by place value:\n```\n  9368\n+  152\n------\n```\n\nStep 2: Add the digits starting from the right:\n- Units: 8 + 2 = 10, write down 0 and carry 1.\n- Tens: 6 + 5 + 1 (carry) = 12, write down 2 and carry 1.\n- Hundreds: 3 + 1 + 1 (carry) = 5, write down 5.\n- Thousands: 9 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 10, write down 0 and carry 1.\n- Ten thousands: 1 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 2.\n\nStep 3: Write the final answer:\n```\n  9368\n+   152\n------\n  9520\n```\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{9520}"}
{"id": "eval-000089", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "clock", "answer": "9:05", "pred": "9:01", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para determinar la hora, observamos las manecillas del reloj. La manecilla de las horas está en la posición de 9, y la manecilla de los minutos está en la posición de 1. Por lo tanto, la hora es 9:01.\n\nLa hora que marca el reloj es **9:01**.\n\n\\boxed{9:01}"}
{"id": "eval-000090", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "counting", "answer": "6", "pred": null, "correct": false, "boxed": false, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para encontrar cuántas estrellas hay en la imagen, veamos cuidadosamente todos los elementos.\n\n- En la parte superior izquierda, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte superior, hay una estrella roja.\n- En la parte superior derecha, hay dos estrellas azules.\n- En la parte inferior izquierda, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella roja.\n- En la parte inferior derecha, hay dos estrellas azules.\n- En la parte central, hay una estrella amarilla.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella roja.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella roja.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella roja.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella roja.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella roja.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella roja.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella roja.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella roja.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella roja.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella roja.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella roja.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella roja.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella roja.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella roja.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella morada.\n- En la parte inferior, hay una estrella roja.\n-"}
{"id": "eval-000091", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "triangle", "answer": "50", "pred": "50^\\circ", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Of course! Let's solve this step by step.\n\nThis is a triangle, and we are given the measures of two of its angles: 68° and 62°. We need to find the value of angle $x$.\n\n### Step 1: Use the Triangle Angle Sum Theorem\nThe sum of the interior angles in any triangle is always 180°. So, we can write:\n$$\n\\text{Sum of angles} = 180^\\circ\n$$\n\n### Step 2: Plug in the known angles\nWe know two angles are 68° and 62°. So:\n$$\n68^\\circ + 62^\\circ + x = 180^\\circ\n$$\n\n### Step 3: Add the known angles\n$$\n68 + 62 = 130\n$$\nSo:\n$$\n130^\\circ + x = 180^\\circ\n$$\n\n### Step 4: Solve for $x$\nSubtract 130° from both sides:\n$$\nx = 180^\\circ - 130^\\circ = 50^\\circ\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:** $\\boxed{50^\\circ}$"}
{"id": "eval-000092", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "column_op", "answer": "6365", "pred": "6365", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To solve the addition problem:\n\n5805 + 560\n\nStep 1: Add the numbers column by column, starting from the right.\n\n- Units place: 5 + 0 = 5\n- Tens place: 0 + 6 = 6\n- Hundreds place: 8 + 5 = 13, write down 3 and carry over 1\n- Thousands place: 5 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 6\n\nSo, 5805 + 560 = 6365.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{6365}"}
{"id": "eval-000093", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "cuboid", "answer": "256", "pred": "256", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the volume of a box, we use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Volume} = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width} \\times \\text{height}\n$$\n\nFrom the image, the dimensions are:\n- Length = 8 m\n- Width = 8 m\n- Height = 4 m\n\nNow, plug in the values:\n\n$$\n\\text{Volume} = 8 \\times 8 \\times 4 = 256 \\text{ m}^3\n$$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{256}$ m³"}
{"id": "eval-000094", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "rectangle", "answer": "70", "pred": "70 \\, \\text{cm}^2", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, con gusto. Para calcular el área de un rectángulo, usamos la fórmula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Área} = \\text{Base} \\times \\text{Altura}\n$$\n\nEn este caso:\n- La base es 10 cm\n- La altura es 7 cm\n\nEntonces:\n\n$$\n\\text{Área} = 10 \\, \\text{cm} \\times 7 \\, \\text{cm} = 70 \\, \\text{cm}^2\n$$\n\nLa respuesta es: $\\boxed{70 \\, \\text{cm}^2}$."}
{"id": "eval-000095", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "numberline", "answer": "5", "pred": "4.5", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "The red point is located exactly in the middle of the number 4 and 5. So, the number is 4.5.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{4.5}$."}
{"id": "eval-000096", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pythagoras", "answer": "7", "pred": "24.69", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "The triangle is a right triangle, so we can use the Pythagorean theorem: $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$, where $c$ is the hypotenuse.\n\nHere, the sides are:\n- One leg is 4 m\n- The hypotenuse is 25 m\n- The other leg is $x$ m\n\nSo, $4^2 + x^2 = 25^2$\n\n$16 + x^2 = 625$\n\n$x^2 = 625 - 16$\n\n$x^2 = 609$\n\n$x = \\sqrt{609}$\n\n$x \\approx 24.69$ m\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{24.69}$ m"}
{"id": "eval-000097", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "circle", "answer": "324\\pi", "pred": "324\\pi", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "¡Claro! Vamos a resolverlo paso a paso.\n\nEl área de un círculo se calcula con la fórmula:\n\n$$\nA = \\pi r^2\n$$\n\nDonde:\n- $A$ es el área,\n- $r$ es el radio del círculo,\n- $\\pi$ es un número constante (aproximadamente 3.1415...).\n\nEn el problema, se nos da el **diametro** (la longitud de la línea que pasa por el centro), que es $d = 36$ m.\n\nEl **radio** $r$ es la mitad del diámetro, así que:\n\n$$\nr = \\frac{36}{2} = 18 \\text{ m}\n$$\n\nAhora, sustituimos $r = 18$ en la fórmula del área:\n\n$$\nA = \\pi \\times (18)^2 = \\pi \\times 324\n$$\n\nEntonces, el área del círculo es:\n\n$$\nA = 324\\pi \\text{ m}^2\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Respuesta final:**\n\n$$\n\\boxed{324\\pi}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000098", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "fraction", "answer": "3/5", "pred": "\\frac{3}{5}", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "La figura está dividida en 5 partes iguales. De estas 5 partes, 3 están coloreadas.\n\nLa fracción que representa las partes coloreadas es:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nEsta fracción ya está en su forma más simple, ya que 3 y 5 no tienen un divisor común mayor que 1.\n\n**Final Answer:** $\\boxed{\\frac{3}{5}}$"}
{"id": "eval-000099", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "cuboid", "answer": "216", "pred": "216 \\text{ m}^2", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Of course! Let's break this down step by step.\n\nThe box is a rectangular prism. The total surface area is the sum of the areas of all six faces.\n\nThe formula for the total surface area of a rectangular prism is:\n$$\n\\text{Surface Area} = 2(lw + lh + wh)\n$$\nwhere:\n- $l$ = length\n- $w$ = width\n- $h$ = height\n\nFrom the image:\n- Length ($l$) = 12 m\n- Width ($w$) = 2 m\n- Height ($h$) = 6 m\n\nNow, plug these values into the formula:\n$$\n\\text{Surface Area} = 2(12 \\times 2 + 12 \\times 6 + 2 \\times 6)\n$$\n\nFirst, calculate each product:\n- $12 \\times 2 = 24$\n- $12 \\times 6 = 72$\n- $2 \\times 6 = 12$\n\nNow add those results:\n- $24 + 72 + 12 = 108$\n\nThen multiply by 2:\n- $2 \\times 108 = 216$\n\nSo, the total surface area is 216 square meters.\n\n$$\n\\boxed{216 \\text{ m}^2}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000100", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "counting", "answer": "3", "pred": "3", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para encontrar cuántas estrellas hay en la imagen, veamos cuidadosamente los objetos que están dibujados.\n\nEn la imagen, podemos ver:\n- Estrellas de color amarillo, morado y naranja.\n\nContemos las estrellas:\n- Una estrella amarilla.\n- Una estrella morada.\n- Una estrella naranja.\n\nHay un total de 3 estrellas.\n\nLa respuesta es: $\\boxed{3}$"}
{"id": "eval-000101", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "counting", "answer": "15", "pred": "13", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the total number of shapes, we need to count each square and star separately and then add them together.\n\n- **Squares**: Let's count the squares.\n  - There are 10 squares in total: 3 in the top row, 2 in the middle, 2 in the bottom, and 1 in the middle-left.\n\n- **Stars**: Let's count the stars.\n  - There are 3 stars: 1 in the middle, 1 on the right, and 1 on the left.\n\nNow, add them together:\n- 10 squares + 3 stars = 13 shapes.\n\nSo, the total number of shapes is 13.\n\n\\boxed{13}"}
{"id": "eval-000102", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "counting", "answer": "8", "pred": "18", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para encontrar cuántos cuadrados hay en la imagen, veamos cuidadosamente los objetos que se ven.\n\n- Hay varios cuadrados de colores diferentes: amarillo, azul, rojo, naranja.\n- Observa que hay 4 cuadrados de color naranja.\n- Hay 2 cuadrados de color rojo.\n- Hay 2 cuadrados de color amarillo.\n- Hay 2 cuadrados de color azul.\n- Hay 2 cuadrados de color naranja.\n- Hay 2 cuadrados de color rojo.\n- Hay 2 cuadrados de color amarillo.\n- Hay 2 cuadrados de color azul.\n\nAhora, sumamos todos los cuadrados: 4 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 2 = 18.\n\nFinalmente, el número total de cuadrados en la imagen es:\n\n\\boxed{18}"}
{"id": "eval-000103", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "cuboid", "answer": "318", "pred": "318", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para hallar el área total de la superficie de la caja, debemos calcular el área de todas sus caras. La caja es un cubo, pero las dimensiones indicadas son 9 m, 7 m y 6 m, lo que sugiere que no es un cubo perfecto. Esto significa que las dimensiones son diferentes, por lo que debemos considerar que es un rectángulo, y el área total de la superficie es la suma de las áreas de todas las caras.\n\nLa caja tiene 6 caras, y cada cara es un rectángulo. El área de una cara es el producto de dos de sus lados. Por lo tanto, el área total de la superficie es:\n\n$$\n2 \\times (9 \\times 7) + 2 \\times (9 \\times 6) + 2 \\times (7 \\times 6)\n$$\n\nCalculamos cada término:\n\n- $9 \\times 7 = 63$\n- $9 \\times 6 = 54$\n- $7 \\times 6 = 42$\n\nEntonces:\n\n$$\n2 \\times 63 = 126\n$$\n$$\n2 \\times 54 = 108\n$$\n$$\n2 \\times 42 = 84\n$$\n\nSumamos:\n\n$$\n126 + 108 + 84 = 318\n$$\n\nLa área total de la superficie de la caja es $318$ m².\n\n$$\n\\boxed{318}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000104", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pie", "answer": "8", "pred": "8", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, aquí tienes la solución paso a paso:\n\n1.  El gráfico muestra que 20 estudiantes fueron encuestados.\n2.  La pregunta es: ¿cuántos eligieron Martes?\n3.  Según el gráfico, el porcentaje de estudiantes que eligieron Martes es 40%.\n4.  Para encontrar el número exacto, multiplicamos el porcentaje por el número total de estudiantes:\n    $ 40\\% \\times 20 = 0.40 \\times 20 = 8 $\n\nPor lo tanto, 8 estudiantes eligieron Martes.\n\n**Respuesta final:** $\\boxed{8}$"}
{"id": "eval-000105", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pythagoras", "answer": "35", "pred": "35", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "The triangle is a right triangle, so we can use the Pythagorean theorem: $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$, where $c$ is the hypotenuse.\n\nHere, the legs are 12 and $x$, and the hypotenuse is 37.\n\nSo, $12^2 + x^2 = 37^2$\n\n$144 + x^2 = 1369$\n\n$x^2 = 1369 - 144$\n\n$x^2 = 1225$\n\n$x = \\sqrt{1225} = 35$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{35}$"}
{"id": "eval-000106", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "sequence", "answer": "25000", "pred": "25000", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Let's look at the sequence: 8, 40, 200, 1000, 5000, ?\n\nFirst, let's look at the pattern in the numbers:\n\n- 8 to 40: 40 ÷ 8 = 5\n- 40 to 200: 200 ÷ 40 = 5\n- 200 to 1000: 1000 ÷ 200 = 5\n- 1000 to 5000: 5000 ÷ 1000 = 5\n\nSo, each number is multiplied by 5 to get the next one.\n\nSo, the next number is 5000 × 5 = 25,000.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{25000}"}
{"id": "eval-000107", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "circle", "answer": "196\\pi", "pred": "196\\pi", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the area of a circle, use the formula:\n\n$$\nA = \\pi r^2\n$$\n\nGiven that the radius $ r = 14 $ m, substitute this value into the formula:\n\n$$\nA = \\pi (14)^2 = \\pi \\times 196\n$$\n\nSo, the area is:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{196\\pi} \\text{ m}^2\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000108", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "barchart", "answer": "6", "pred": "6", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To solve this, look at the bar chart. The vertical axis shows the number of votes, and the horizontal axis shows the different sports.\n\n1.  Find the bar labeled \"Soccer\".\n2.  Look at the height of the bar for Soccer. The bar goes up to the number 6 on the vertical axis.\n3.  So, Soccer has 6 votes.\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{6}$"}
{"id": "eval-000109", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "barchart", "answer": "5", "pred": "5", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para calcular la media, primero necesitamos encontrar el total de los votos y luego dividirlo entre el número de categorías.\n\n- Votos de Perros: 9\n- Votos de Gatos: 2\n- Votos de Peces: 3\n- Votos de Pájaros: 6\n\nSuma de los votos: 9 + 2 + 3 + 6 = 20\n\nNúmero de categorías: 4\n\nMedia = 20 / 4 = 5\n\nLa media de los votos es 5.\n\n\\boxed{5}"}
{"id": "eval-000110", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "clock", "answer": "6:20", "pred": "6:20", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the time in 10 minutes, we start by looking at the current time on the clock.\n\n- The hour hand is pointing at 6, which means it is 6:00.\n- The minute hand is pointing at 2, which means it is 10 minutes past the hour.\n\nSo, the current time is 6:10.\n\nIn 10 minutes, we add 10 minutes to the current time.\n\n6:10 + 10 minutes = 6:20.\n\nTherefore, the time will be 6:20.\n\n\\boxed{6:20}"}
