{"id": "eval-000166", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pythagoras", "answer": "20", "pred": "10\\sqrt{6}", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "El triángulo es rectángulo, por lo que podemos usar el teorema de Pitágoras. El teorema de Pitágoras establece que en un triángulo rectángulo, el cuadrado de la hipotenusa (el lado más largo) es igual a la suma de los cuadrados de los otros dos lados.\n\nEn este caso:\n- La hipotenusa es de 25 m.\n- Un lado es de 5 m.\n- El otro lado es $ x $.\n\nAplicando el teorema:\n$$\nx^2 + 5^2 = 25^2\n$$\n$$\nx^2 + 25 = 625\n$$\n$$\nx^2 = 625 - 25 = 600\n$$\n$$\nx = \\sqrt{600} = \\sqrt{100 \\times 6} = 10\\sqrt{6}\n$$\n\nFinalmente, la respuesta es:\n$$\n\\boxed{10\\sqrt{6}} \\text{ m}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000167", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "sequence", "answer": "2048", "pred": "2048", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Analicemos la sucesión: 2, 8, 32, 128, 512, ?\n\nVeamos los números:\n- 2 = 2\n- 8 = 2 × 4\n- 32 = 8 × 4\n- 128 = 32 × 4\n- 512 = 128 × 4\n\nPuedes ver que cada número es el anterior multiplicado por 4.\n\nEntonces:\n- 512 × 4 = 2048\n\nLa sucesión es: 2, 8, 32, 128, 512, **2048**\n\n\\boxed{2048}"}
{"id": "eval-000168", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "rectangle", "answer": "48", "pred": "48 \\, \\text{cm}^2", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "¡Claro! Vamos a resolverlo paso a paso.\n\nEl área de un rectángulo se calcula con la fórmula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Área} = \\text{Ancho} \\times \\text{Alto}\n$$\n\nEn este caso:\n- El ancho es 4 cm\n- El alto es 12 cm\n\nEntonces:\n\n$$\n\\text{Área} = 4 \\, \\text{cm} \\times 12 \\, \\text{cm} = 48 \\, \\text{cm}^2\n$$\n\n**Respuesta final:**\n$$\n\\boxed{48 \\, \\text{cm}^2}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000169", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "fraction", "answer": "2/3", "pred": "\\frac{4}{5}", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "La figura está dividida en 5 partes iguales. De estas 5 partes, 4 están coloreadas.\n\nLa fracción que representa las partes coloreadas es:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5}\n$$\n\nEsta fracción ya está en su forma más simple, ya que 4 y 5 no tienen un divisor común mayor que 1.\n\n**Final Answer:** $\\boxed{\\frac{4}{5}}$"}
{"id": "eval-000170", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "clock", "answer": "3:50", "pred": "10:10", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, aquí tienes la solución paso a paso:\n\n1.  **Observa la hora en la manecilla del reloj.**\n    - La manecilla de las horas está en la posición de **10**.\n    - La manecilla de los minutos está en la posición de **10**.\n    - La manecilla de las horas está en la posición de **10**.\n    - La manecilla de los minutos está en la posición de **10**.\n\n2.  **Determina la hora.**\n    - La manecilla de las horas está en la posición de **10**.\n    - La manecilla de los minutos está en la posición de **10**.\n    - La manecilla de las horas está en la posición de **10**.\n    - La manecilla de los minutos está en la posición de **10**.\n\n3.  **Conclusión:**\n    - La hora es **10:10**.\n\nFinalmente, la hora que marca el reloj es:\n\n\\boxed{10:10}"}
{"id": "eval-000171", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "barchart", "answer": "4", "pred": "4", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find how many more votes Baseball has than Soccer, subtract the number of votes for Soccer from the number of votes for Baseball.\n\n- Number of votes for Baseball: 14\n- Number of votes for Soccer: 10\n\nNow, subtract:  \n14 - 10 = 4\n\nSo, Baseball has 4 more votes than Soccer.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{4}"}
{"id": "eval-000172", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "circle", "answer": "36\\pi", "pred": "36\\pi", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the circumference of a circle, use the formula:\n\n$$ C = \\pi \\times d $$\n\nwhere $ C $ is the circumference and $ d $ is the diameter.\n\nGiven that the diameter $ d = 36 $ meters, substitute this into the formula:\n\n$$ C = \\pi \\times 36 $$\n\nSo, the circumference is $ 36\\pi $ meters.\n\nFinal answer: $ \\boxed{36\\pi} $ meters."}
{"id": "eval-000173", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pie", "answer": "60", "pred": "60", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, vamos a resolver esto paso a paso.\n\n1.  El gráfico es un diagrama de barras porcentuales, que muestra las proporciones de las preferencias de los estudiantes.\n2.  Según el gráfico, el porcentaje de estudiantes que eligieron **Uvas** es del 50%.\n3.  Se preguntó a un total de **120 estudiantes**.\n4.  Para encontrar cuántos eligieron uvas, multiplicamos el porcentaje de uvas por el número total de estudiantes:\n\n    $ 50\\% \\times 120 = \\frac{50}{100} \\times 120 = 0.5 \\times 120 = 60 $\n\nEntonces, **60 estudiantes** eligieron uvas.\n\n\\boxed{60}"}
{"id": "eval-000174", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pie", "answer": "32", "pred": "32", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find how many students chose Baseball, follow these steps:\n\n1.  The pie chart shows the percentage of students who chose each sport.\n2.  The percentage for Baseball is 40%.\n3.  To find the number of students, multiply the total number of students by the percentage for Baseball.\n\n$$ 80 \\times 0.40 = 32 $$\n\nSo, 32 students chose Baseball.\n\n$\\boxed{32}$"}
{"id": "eval-000175", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "cuboid", "answer": "182", "pred": "182", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the total surface area of the box, we need to calculate the area of all six faces.\n\nThe box is a rectangular prism with dimensions:\n- Length = 7 m\n- Width = 7 m\n- Height = 3 m\n\nThe surface area of a rectangular prism is given by:\n$$\n\\text{Surface Area} = 2(lw + lh + wh)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the values:\n$$\n\\text{Surface Area} = 2(7 \\times 7 + 7 \\times 3 + 7 \\times 3)\n$$\n\nCalculate each product:\n- $7 \\times 7 = 49$\n- $7 \\times 3 = 21$\n- $7 \\times 3 = 21$\n\nNow add:\n$$\n49 + 21 + 21 = 91\n$$\n\nMultiply by 2:\n$$\n2 \\times 91 = 182\n$$\n\nSo, the total surface area is 182 square meters.\n\n$$\n\\boxed{182} \\text{ m}^2\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000176", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "rectangle", "answer": "18", "pred": "18", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the perimeter of a rectangle, we use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Perimeter} = 2 \\times (\\text{length} + \\text{width})\n$$\n\nFrom the image, the length is 4 cm and the width is 5 cm.\n\n$$\n\\text{Perimeter} = 2 \\times (4 + 5) = 2 \\times 9 = 18 \\text{ cm}\n$$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{18}$ cm"}
{"id": "eval-000177", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "triangle", "answer": "50", "pred": "50^\\circ", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para hallar el valor del ángulo $ x $, usamos la suma de los ángulos internos de un triángulo, que siempre suma $ 180^\\circ $.\n\nDado:\n- Un ángulo es $ 37^\\circ $\n- Otro ángulo es $ 93^\\circ $\n- El tercer ángulo es $ x $\n\nEntonces:\n$$\nx = 180^\\circ - 37^\\circ - 93^\\circ\n$$\n\nCalculamos:\n$$\nx = 180 - 37 - 93 = 180 - 130 = 50^\\circ\n$$\n\nFinalmente:\n$$\n\\boxed{50^\\circ}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000178", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "cuboid", "answer": "540", "pred": "540 \\text{ m}^3", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Of course! To find the volume of a box, we use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Volume} = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width} \\times \\text{height}\n$$\n\nFrom the image, the dimensions are:\n- Length = 12 m\n- Width = 9 m\n- Height = 5 m\n\nNow, plug these values into the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Volume} = 12 \\times 9 \\times 5\n$$\n\nFirst, multiply 12 and 9:\n\n$$\n12 \\times 9 = 108\n$$\n\nThen multiply by 5:\n\n$$\n108 \\times 5 = 540\n$$\n\nSo, the volume of the box is 540 cubic meters.\n\n$$\n\\boxed{540 \\text{ m}^3}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000179", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "circle", "answer": "34\\pi", "pred": "34\\pi", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para hallar la longitud de la circunferencia, usamos la fórmula:\n\n\\[\nC = \\pi \\times d\n\\]\n\nDonde \\( d \\) es el diámetro. En este caso, el diámetro es 34 cm.\n\n\\[\nC = \\pi \\times 34\n\\]\n\n\\[\nC = 34\\pi \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nFinalmente, la longitud de la circunferencia es:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{34\\pi} \\text{ cm}\n\\]"}
{"id": "eval-000180", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "triangle", "answer": "82", "pred": "82^\\circ", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the value of angle $x$, we can use the fact that the sum of the interior angles in any triangle is $180^\\circ$.\n\nGiven angles:\n- $30^\\circ$\n- $68^\\circ$\n- $x$\n\nSo:\n$$\n30^\\circ + 68^\\circ + x = 180^\\circ\n$$\n\nAdd the known angles:\n$$\n98^\\circ + x = 180^\\circ\n$$\n\nSolve for $x$:\n$$\nx = 180^\\circ - 98^\\circ = 82^\\circ\n$$\n\nFinal answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{82^\\circ}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000181", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pythagoras", "answer": "16", "pred": "6\\sqrt{11}", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "El triángulo es rectángulo, por lo que es un triángulo rectángulo con un ángulo de 90°. Usamos el teorema de Pitágoras para hallar el valor de x.\n\nEl teorema de Pitágoras dice que en un triángulo rectángulo:  \n$$\na^2 + b^2 = c^2\n$$  \ndonde $c$ es la hipotenusa (el lado opuesto al ángulo recto) y $a$ y $b$ son los otros dos lados.\n\nEn este caso:\n- La hipotenusa es 20 cm.\n- Un lado es 2 cm.\n- El otro lado es $x$.\n\nEntonces:\n$$\nx^2 + 2^2 = 20^2\n$$\n$$\nx^2 + 4 = 400\n$$\n$$\nx^2 = 400 - 4 = 396\n$$\n$$\nx = \\sqrt{396}\n$$\n$$\nx = \\sqrt{4 \\times 99} = 2\\sqrt{99}\n$$\n\nPero podemos simplificar $\\sqrt{396}$:\n$$\n\\sqrt{396} = \\sqrt{4 \\times 99} = 2\\sqrt{99}\n$$\n\nPero $99 = 9 \\times 11$, así que:\n$$\n\\sqrt{396} = 2\\sqrt{9 \\times 11} = 2 \\times 3 \\times \\sqrt{11} = 6\\sqrt{11}\n$$\n\nEntonces:\n$$\nx = 6\\sqrt{11}\n$$\n\nFinalmente:\n$$\n\\boxed{6\\sqrt{11}} \\text{ cm}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000182", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "equation", "answer": "1", "pred": "1", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Of course! Let's solve the equation step by step.\n\nThe equation is:\n$$3(x - 9) = -24$$\n\n**Step 1: Distribute the 3.**\nMultiply 3 by each term inside the parentheses:\n$$3 \\cdot x - 3 \\cdot 9 = -24$$\n$$3x - 27 = -24$$\n\n**Step 2: Add 27 to both sides.**\nThis isolates the term with x:\n$$3x = -24 + 27$$\n$$3x = 3$$\n\n**Step 3: Divide both sides by 3.**\n$$x = \\frac{3}{3}$$\n$$x = 1$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x = 1$.\n\n$\\boxed{1}$"}
{"id": "eval-000183", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "circle", "answer": "42\\pi", "pred": "42\\pi", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the circumference of a circle, use the formula:\n\n$$\nC = 2\\pi r\n$$\n\nGiven that the radius $ r = 21 $ cm, substitute this value into the formula:\n\n$$\nC = 2\\pi \\times 21 = 42\\pi \\text{ cm}\n$$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{42\\pi}$ cm"}
{"id": "eval-000184", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "rectangle", "answer": "30", "pred": "30", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para encontrar el perímetro de un rectángulo, usamos la fórmula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Perímetro} = 2 \\times (\\text{ancho} + \\text{altura})\n$$\n\nEn este caso:\n- Ancho = 6 m\n- Altura = 9 m\n\nSustituyendo:\n\n$$\n\\text{Perímetro} = 2 \\times (6 + 9) = 2 \\times 15 = 30 \\text{ m}\n$$\n\nFinalmente:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{30} \\text{ m}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000185", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "numberline", "answer": "30", "pred": "45", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Of course! Let's solve this step by step.\n\n1.  The number line goes from 10 to 80.\n2.  The red dot is located exactly in the middle of the line.\n3.  The line is divided into 10 equal parts between 10 and 80.\n4.  The total span is 80 - 10 = 70 units.\n5.  There are 10 equal parts, so each part is 70 ÷ 10 = 7 units.\n6.  The red dot is at the 5th mark from the left, which is 10 + 5 × 7 = 10 + 35 = 45.\n\nThe red point marks the number 45.\n\n\\boxed{45}"}
{"id": "eval-000186", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "circle", "answer": "49\\pi", "pred": "49\\pi", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the area of a circle, use the formula:\n\n$$\nA = \\pi r^2\n$$\n\nwhere $ r $ is the radius of the circle.\n\nWe are given the diameter $ d = 14 $ m. The radius $ r $ is half of the diameter:\n\n$$\nr = \\frac{14}{2} = 7 \\text{ m}\n$$\n\nNow substitute $ r = 7 $ into the area formula:\n\n$$\nA = \\pi (7)^2 = \\pi \\cdot 49\n$$\n\nSo, the area is:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{49\\pi} \\text{ m}^2\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000187", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "sequence", "answer": "58", "pred": "58", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Let's look at the sequence: 43, 46, 49, 52, 55, ?\n\nFirst, look at the differences between consecutive numbers:\n- 46 - 43 = 3\n- 49 - 46 = 3\n- 52 - 49 = 3\n- 55 - 52 = 3\n\nThe difference between each number is 3. So, the pattern is that each number increases by 3.\n\nSo, the next number is:\n55 + 3 = 58\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{58}"}
{"id": "eval-000188", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pie", "answer": "18", "pred": "18", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, vamos a resolver esto paso a paso.\n\n1.  La imagen muestra un gráfico de barras porcentuales. El gráfico indica que:\n    - Fútbol: 15%\n    - Béisbol: 50%\n    - Natación: 25%\n    - Tenis: 10%\n\n2.  Se preguntó a 120 estudiantes. Para saber cuántos eligieron Fútbol, debemos calcular el 15% de 120.\n\n3.  Calculamos:  \n    $ 15\\% \\times 120 = \\frac{15}{100} \\times 120 = 0.15 \\times 120 = 18 $\n\nEntonces, 18 estudiantes eligieron Fútbol.\n\n**Respuesta final:** $\\boxed{18}$"}
{"id": "eval-000189", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "counting", "answer": "15", "pred": null, "correct": false, "boxed": false, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Of course! Let's break it down step by step.\n\nThe question asks: **\"How many shapes are there in total (stars and triangles)?\"**\n\nWe need to count all the **triangles** and **stars** in the image.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Count the triangles\nLook at the triangles in the image.\n\n- In the top left, there is 1 yellow triangle.\n- Below that, there are 2 more triangles: one green and one blue.\n- In the middle, there is 1 purple triangle.\n- In the bottom, there is 1 green triangle, 1 orange triangle, and 1 more triangle.\n\nLet's count them:\n- 1 (yellow) + 2 (green, blue) + 1 (purple) + 1 (green) + 1 (orange) = 6 triangles.\n\nWait, let's double-check:\n- Top: 1 triangle\n- Middle: 1 triangle\n- Bottom: 3 triangles\n- Total: 1 + 1 + 3 = 5 triangles.\n\nWait, let's count again carefully:\n- Top: 1 yellow triangle\n- Middle: 1 purple triangle\n- Bottom: 3 triangles (green, blue, orange)\n- So: 1 + 1 + 3 = 5 triangles.\n\nYes, that's 5 triangles.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Count the stars\nNow, count the stars.\n\n- Top right: 1 red star\n- Middle: 1 yellow star\n- Right side: 2 stars (one orange, one red)\n- Bottom: 2 stars (one orange, one red)\n\nWait, let's count again:\n- Top: 1 red star\n- Middle: 1 yellow star\n- Right: 2 stars (one orange, one red)\n- Bottom: 2 stars (one orange, one red)\n\nWait, no, let's look again.\n\nActually, let's go through the image carefully.\n\n- Top: 1 yellow triangle\n- Middle: 1 purple triangle\n- Bottom: 3 triangles (green, blue, orange)\n- So triangles: 1 + 1 + 3 = 5\n\nNow stars:\n- Top: 1 red star\n- Middle: 1 yellow star\n- Right: 2 stars (one orange, one red)\n- Bottom: 2 stars (one orange, one red)\n\nWait, no, let's count the stars in the image.\n\nLooking"}
{"id": "eval-000190", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pythagoras", "answer": "37", "pred": "\\sqrt{1229}", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Of course! This is a right triangle, so we can use the Pythagorean theorem: $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$, where $c$ is the hypotenuse.\n\nIn this triangle:\n- One leg is 2 cm.\n- The other leg is 35 cm.\n- The hypotenuse is $x$.\n\nSo, we can write:\n$$\n2^2 + 35^2 = x^2\n$$\n\nNow, calculate:\n$$\n4 + 1225 = x^2\n$$\n$$\n1229 = x^2\n$$\n\nTake the square root of both sides:\n$$\nx = \\sqrt{1229}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $x$ is $\\sqrt{1229}$ cm.\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{\\sqrt{1229}}$ cm."}
{"id": "eval-000191", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "equation", "answer": "-8", "pred": null, "correct": false, "boxed": false, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Of course! Here's how to solve the equation step by step:\n\n1.  **Distribute the 4**: Multiply 4 by each term inside the parentheses.\n    $4(x - 5) = 4x - 20$\n\n2.  **Write the equation**:\n    $4x - 20 = -52$\n\n3.  **Add 20 to both sides** to isolate the term with $x$.\n    $4x = -52 + 20$\n    $4x = -32$\n\n4.  **Divide both sides by 4** to solve for $x$.\n    $x = -32 / 4$\n    $x = -8$\n\nSo, the solution is $x = -8$."}
{"id": "eval-000192", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "column_op", "answer": "1770", "pred": "1770", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To solve the multiplication problem:\n\n885 × 2\n\nWe can multiply each digit of 885 by 2, starting from the right:\n\n- 5 × 2 = 10, write down 0 and carry 1.\n- 8 × 2 = 16, plus the carried 1 = 17, write down 17.\n- 8 × 2 = 16, plus the carried 1 = 17, write down 17.\n\nSo, 885 × 2 = 1770.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{1770}"}
{"id": "eval-000193", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "barchart", "answer": "185", "pred": "185", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, veamos el gráfico.\n\nEl gráfico es un diagrama de barras que muestra los votos de la clase para diferentes frutas.\n\n- Las frutas son: Manzanas, Peras, Uvas, y Mangos.\n- El eje vertical muestra el número de votos.\n- Las barras indican el número de votos para cada fruta.\n\nPara encontrar el número total de votos, sumamos los votos de cada fruta:\n\n- Manzanas: 50 votos\n- Peras: 50 votos\n- Uvas: 45 votos\n- Mangos: 40 votos\n\nAhora, sumamos:\n\n50 + 50 + 45 + 40 = 185\n\nEl número total de votos es 185.\n\n\\boxed{185}"}
{"id": "eval-000194", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pie", "answer": "12", "pred": "12", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To solve this, follow these steps:\n\n1.  The pie chart shows the percentage of students who chose each day.\n2.  The total number of students is 60.\n3.  Find the percentage for Thursday, which is 20%.\n4.  To find how many students chose Thursday, multiply the total number of students by the percentage for Thursday.\n    - 20% of 60 = 0.20 × 60 = 12\n\nSo, 12 students chose Thursday.\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{12}$"}
{"id": "eval-000195", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "triangle", "answer": "68", "pred": "68^\\circ", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "En un triángulo, la suma de los tres ángulos es siempre 180°.  \nDado que los otros dos ángulos son 44° y 68°, podemos hallar el valor de x:  \n\nx = 180° - 44° - 68°  \nx = 180° - 112°  \nx = 68°  \n\n**Respuesta final:** \\boxed{68^\\circ}"}
{"id": "eval-000196", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "slope", "answer": "2/3", "pred": "\\frac{2}{3}", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the slope of the line through the two points, use the slope formula:\n\n$$\nm = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}\n$$\n\nThe two points are:\n- $(-2, 0)$\n- $(1, 2)$\n\nSubstitute the values:\n- $x_1 = -2$, $y_1 = 0$\n- $x_2 = 1$, $y_2 = 2$\n\n$$\nm = \\frac{2 - 0}{1 - (-2)} = \\frac{2}{1 + 2} = \\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{\\frac{2}{3}}$"}
{"id": "eval-000197", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "triangle", "answer": "58", "pred": "58^\\circ", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the value of angle $x$, we can use the fact that the sum of the interior angles in a triangle is always $180^\\circ$.\n\nGiven angles:\n- $40^\\circ$\n- $82^\\circ$\n- $x$\n\nSo:\n$$\n40^\\circ + 82^\\circ + x = 180^\\circ\n$$\n\nAdd the known angles:\n$$\n122^\\circ + x = 180^\\circ\n$$\n\nNow solve for $x$:\n$$\nx = 180^\\circ - 122^\\circ = 58^\\circ\n$$\n\nFinal answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{58^\\circ}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000198", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "barchart", "answer": "27", "pred": "27", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para encontrar el número total de votos, sumamos los votos de cada categoría:\n\n- Perros: 9 votos\n- Gatos: 10 votos\n- Peces: 4 votos\n- Pájaros: 2 votos\n- Conejos: 2 votos\n\nSuma: 9 + 10 + 4 + 2 + 2 = 27\n\nEl número total de votos es 27.\n\n\\boxed{27}"}
{"id": "eval-000199", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "equation", "answer": "-6", "pred": "-6", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To solve for $x$, follow these steps:\n\n1. Subtract 19 from both sides of the equation:\n   $6x + 19 = -17$\n   $6x = -17 - 19$\n   $6x = -36$\n\n2. Divide both sides by 6:\n   $x = \\frac{-36}{6}$\n   $x = -6$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{-6}$"}
{"id": "eval-000200", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pythagoras", "answer": "106", "pred": "90.2", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "El triángulo es rectángulo, por lo que podemos usar el teorema de Pitágoras. El teorema de Pitágoras establece que en un triángulo rectángulo, el cuadrado de la hipotenusa (la lado más largo) es igual a la suma de los cuadrados de los otros dos lados.\n\nEn este caso:\n- La hipotenusa es $ x $.\n- Un lado es $ 6 $ m.\n- El otro lado es $ 90 $ m.\n\nAplicando el teorema:\n$$\nx^2 = 6^2 + 90^2\n$$\n$$\nx^2 = 36 + 8100\n$$\n$$\nx^2 = 8136\n$$\n$$\nx = \\sqrt{8136}\n$$\n\nCalculamos la raíz cuadrada:\n$$\nx = \\sqrt{8136} = 90.2\n$$\n\nPor lo tanto, el valor de $ x $ es $ \\boxed{90.2} $ m."}
{"id": "eval-000201", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "clock", "answer": "12:10", "pred": "12:10", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "La hora actual es las 11:30. Dentro de 40 minutos, será las 12:10.\n\n**Solución paso a paso:**\n1.  La hora actual es las 11:30.\n2.  Sumamos 40 minutos a la hora actual: 30 minutos + 40 minutos = 70 minutos.\n3.  70 minutos son 1 hora y 10 minutos.\n4.  11:30 + 1:10 = 12:10.\n\nLa hora será **12:10**.\n\n\\boxed{12:10}"}
{"id": "eval-000202", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "column_op", "answer": "6643", "pred": "6643", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To solve the multiplication problem:\n\n949 × 7\n\nWe can break it down step by step:\n\nFirst, multiply 949 by 7:\n\n- 7 × 9 = 63\n- 7 × 40 = 280\n- 7 × 90 = 630\n\nWait, let's do it properly:\n\nWe can do it column by column:\n\n7 × 949\n\n7 × 900 = 6300  \n7 × 40 = 280  \n7 × 9 = 63\n\nNow add them together:\n\n6300 + 280 = 6580  \n6580 + 63 = 6643\n\nSo, 949 × 7 = 6643\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{6643}"}
{"id": "eval-000203", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pythagoras", "answer": "16", "pred": "16", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "El triángulo es rectángulo, por lo que podemos usar el teorema de Pitágoras. El teorema de Pitágoras establece que en un triángulo rectángulo, el cuadrado de la hipotenusa (la lado más largo) es igual a la suma de los cuadrados de los otros dos lados.\n\nEn este caso:\n- La hipotenusa es el lado de 20.\n- Los otros dos lados son 12 y x.\n\nAplicando el teorema:\n$$\nx^2 + 12^2 = 20^2\n$$\n\nCalculamos:\n$$\nx^2 + 144 = 400\n$$\n\nRestamos 144 de ambos lados:\n$$\nx^2 = 400 - 144 = 256\n$$\n\nTomamos la raíz cuadrada:\n$$\nx = \\sqrt{256} = 16\n$$\n\nFinalmente:\n$$\n\\boxed{16}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000204", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pie", "answer": "4", "pred": "4", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find how many students chose Monday, follow these steps:\n\n1.  The pie chart shows the percentage of students who chose each day.\n2.  Monday is represented by the red slice, which is 10%.\n3.  We need to find 10% of the total number of students, which is 40.\n\nCalculate:\n$ 10\\% \\times 40 = \\frac{10}{100} \\times 40 = 0.10 \\times 40 = 4 $\n\nSo, 4 students chose Monday.\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{4}$"}
{"id": "eval-000205", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "barchart", "answer": "20", "pred": "20", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To solve this, we need to find the difference in the number of votes between Tuesday and Wednesday.\n\n1.  First, look at the bar chart. The vertical axis (y-axis) shows the number of votes.\n2.  Find the bar for Tuesday. It is the second bar from the left. The height of the bar is above the 25 mark, so Tuesday has 25 votes.\n3.  Find the bar for Wednesday. It is the third bar from the left. The height of the bar is below the 5 mark, so Wednesday has 5 votes.\n4.  Now, subtract the number of votes for Wednesday from the number of votes for Tuesday: 25 - 5 = 20.\n\nSo, Tuesday has 20 more votes than Wednesday.\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{20}$"}
{"id": "eval-000206", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "fraction", "answer": "3/4", "pred": "\\frac{3}{4}", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the fraction of the shape that is shaded, follow these steps:\n\n1.  **Count the total number of equal parts:** The circle is divided into 4 equal parts by the lines. So, the total number of parts is 4.\n\n2.  **Count the shaded parts:** Out of these 4 parts, 3 are shaded.\n\n3.  **Write the fraction:** The fraction of the shape that is shaded is $\\frac{3}{4}$.\n\n4.  **Simplify:** The fraction $\\frac{3}{4}$ is already in its simplest form.\n\nSo, the final answer is $\\boxed{\\frac{3}{4}}$."}
