{"id": "eval-000209", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "column_op", "answer": "311", "pred": "311", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To solve this, we need to subtract 617 from 928.\n\nWe can do this by aligning the numbers vertically and subtracting digit by digit from right to left.\n\n```\n   928\n -  617\n-------\n```\n\nStart from the ones place:\n- 8 - 7 = 1\n\nNext, the tens place:\n- 2 - 1 = 1\n\nFinally, the hundreds place:\n- 9 - 6 = 3\n\nPutting it all together:\n- 928 - 617 = 311\n\nSo, the final answer is $\\boxed{311}$."}
{"id": "eval-000210", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pie", "answer": "6", "pred": "6", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, vamos a resolver esto paso a paso.\n\n1.  El gráfico muestra las proporciones de las preferencias de los estudiantes.\n2.  La pregunta es: ¿Cuántos de los 60 estudiantes eligieron manzanas?\n3.  Según el gráfico, el porcentaje de estudiantes que eligieron manzanas es del 10%.\n4.  Para encontrar cuántos estudiantes eligieron manzanas, multiplicamos el porcentaje por el número total de estudiantes:\n    - 10% de 60 = (10/100) × 60 = 0.10 × 60 = 6\n\nEntonces, 6 estudiantes eligieron manzanas.\n\n**Final de la respuesta:**\n\\boxed{6}"}
{"id": "eval-000211", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pythagoras", "answer": "41", "pred": "41", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "¡Claro! Aquí tienes los pasos para resolver el problema:\n\n1.  El triángulo es rectángulo, lo que significa que tiene un ángulo de 90°. Por lo tanto, es un triángulo rectángulo con un lado de 40, otro de 9, y la hipotenusa (la lado opuesto al ángulo recto) que es el lado que buscamos, que está marcado con \"x\".\n\n2.  Usamos el **Teorema de Pitágoras**, que dice que en un triángulo rectángulo, el cuadrado de la hipotenusa es igual a la suma de los cuadrados de los otros dos lados.\n\n3.  Aplicamos la fórmula:\n    $$\n    x^2 = 40^2 + 9^2\n    $$\n\n4.  Calculamos:\n    $$\n    x^2 = 1600 + 81 = 1681\n    $$\n\n5.  Para hallar x, tomamos la raíz cuadrada:\n    $$\n    x = \\sqrt{1681} = 41\n    $$\n\n**Respuesta final:**\n$$\n\\boxed{41}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000212", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "numberline", "answer": "-1", "pred": "-1", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "La recta numérica muestra que el punto rojo está ubicado justo a la derecha de -1. Observa que el punto está en la posición que representa el número -1, y el punto rojo está sobre el número -1. Por lo tanto, el número que marca el punto rojo es -1.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{-1}"}
{"id": "eval-000213", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "cuboid", "answer": "250", "pred": "250", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para hallar el volumen de una caja, usamos la fórmula:\n\n$$\nV = \\text{ancho} \\times \\text{alto} \\times \\text{profundidad}\n$$\n\nDe la imagen, tenemos:\n- Ancho = 10 cm\n- Alto = 5 cm\n- Profundidad = 5 cm\n\nSustituyendo:\n\n$$\nV = 10 \\times 5 \\times 5 = 250 \\text{ cm}^3\n$$\n\nFinalmente, el volumen de la caja es:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{250} \\text{ cm}^3\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000214", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "slope", "answer": "-2", "pred": "-2", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the slope of the line through the two points, use the slope formula:\n\n$$\nm = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}\n$$\n\nGiven points:  \n- $ (x_1, y_1) = (-1, 3) $  \n- $ (x_2, y_2) = (2, -3) $\n\nSubstitute the values into the formula:\n\n$$\nm = \\frac{-3 - 3}{2 - (-1)} = \\frac{-6}{2 - (-1)} = \\frac{-6}{2 + 1} = \\frac{-6}{3} = -2\n$$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{-2}$"}
{"id": "eval-000215", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "clock", "answer": "12:50", "pred": "12:50", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "The clock shows the time is 11:35. In 75 minutes, it will be 11:35 + 75 minutes.\n\n75 minutes is 1 hour and 15 minutes. So, 11:35 + 1 hour = 12:35, and 12:35 + 15 minutes = 12:50.\n\nThe final answer is \\boxed{12:50}."}
{"id": "eval-000216", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pie", "answer": "4", "pred": "4", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find how many students chose Thursday, follow these steps:\n\n1.  The pie chart shows the percentage of students who chose each day.\n2.  The percentage for Thursday is 20%.\n3.  The total number of students is 20.\n4.  To find the number of students who chose Thursday, calculate 20% of 20.\n\n   $ 20\\% \\times 20 = \\frac{20}{100} \\times 20 = 0.20 \\times 20 = 4 $\n\nSo, 4 students chose Thursday.\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{4}$"}
{"id": "eval-000217", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "clock", "answer": "8:55", "pred": "9:10", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To read the time on the clock, we look at the positions of the hands.\n\n- The hour hand is pointing just past the 9, so it's 9:00.\n- The minute hand is pointing at the 10, which is 10 minutes past the hour.\n\nSo, the time is 9:10.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{9:10}$."}
{"id": "eval-000218", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "fraction", "answer": "1/2", "pred": "\\frac{1}{2}", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, veamos el ejercicio paso a paso.\n\n1.  **Identificar la parte coloreada:** La figura es una línea recta que está dividida en dos partes iguales. La parte izquierda es blanca y la parte derecha es naranja. Solo la mitad derecha está coloreada.\n\n2.  **Escribir la fracción:** La fracción que representa la parte coloreada es la parte que está coloreada dividida entre el total de partes. El total de partes es 2. La parte coloreada es 1 de las 2 partes.\n\n3.  **Simplificar:** La fracción es $\\frac{1}{2}$. Esta fracción ya está en su forma más simple, ya que el número 1 no puede dividirse por ningún número natural mayor que 1.\n\nPor lo tanto, la fracción de la figura que está coloreada es $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}"}
{"id": "eval-000219", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "counting", "answer": "15", "pred": null, "correct": false, "boxed": false, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "¡Claro! Vamos a resolverlo paso a paso.\n\nEl ejercicio es: **¿Cuántas figuras hay en total entre cuadrados y círculos?**\n\nPrimero, debemos contar **cuadrados** y **círculos** separadamente.\n\n---\n\n### Paso 1: Contar los cuadrados\n\nEn la imagen, veamos los cuadrados:\n\n- En la parte superior izquierda: 1 cuadrado naranja.\n- En la parte inferior izquierda: 1 cuadrado rojo.\n- En la parte inferior: 1 cuadrado verde.\n- En la parte inferior: 1 cuadrado amarillo.\n- En la parte inferior: 1 cuadrado azul.\n\n¡Ah! Hay **5 cuadrados**.\n\n---\n\n### Paso 2: Contar los círculos\n\nAhora, los círculos:\n\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo rojo.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo azul.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo amarillo.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo naranja.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo azul.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo rojo.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo azul.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo amarillo.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo azul.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo rojo.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo azul.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo amarillo.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo azul.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo rojo.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo azul.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo amarillo.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo azul.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo rojo.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo azul.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo amarillo.\n- En la parte superior: 1 círculo azul.\n"}
{"id": "eval-000220", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "barchart", "answer": "38", "pred": "30", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para encontrar el número total de votos, sumamos los votos de cada categoría:\n\n- Perros: 6 votos\n- Gatos: 4 votos\n- Peces: 2 votos\n- Pájaros: 8 votos\n- Conejos: 18 votos\n\nSuma: 6 + 4 + 2 + 8 + 18 = 30\n\nEl número total de votos es 30.\n\n\\boxed{30}"}
{"id": "eval-000221", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "cuboid", "answer": "96", "pred": "96", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para hallar el volumen de un rectángulo, usamos la fórmula:\n\n$$\nV = \\text{ancho} \\times \\text{altura} \\times \\text{longitud}\n$$\n\nEn el problema, los valores dados son:\n\n- Ancho = 12 cm\n- Altura = 4 cm\n- Longitud = 2 cm\n\nSustituyendo:\n\n$$\nV = 12 \\times 4 \\times 2 = 96 \\text{ cm}^3\n$$\n\nFinalmente, el volumen de la caja es:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{96} \\text{cm}^3\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000222", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "prices", "answer": "27.50", "pred": "27.50", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, aquí tienes la solución paso a paso:\n\n1.  **Identificar los precios:**\n    - Precio de una manzana: $1.25\n    - Precio de un cuaderno: $4.00\n    - Precio de un borrador: $0.75\n    - Precio de jugo: $2.00\n\n2.  **Calcular el costo total:**\n    - Ana compra 6 manzanas y 5 cuadernos.\n    - Costo de las manzanas: $1.25 \\times 6 = 7.50$\n    - Costo de los cuadernos: $4.00 \\times 5 = 20.00$\n    - Total: $7.50 + 20.00 = 27.50$\n\n3.  **Respuesta final:**\n    Ana paga un total de $27.50.\n\n\\boxed{27.50}"}
{"id": "eval-000223", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pie", "answer": "4", "pred": "4", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, aquí tienes la solución paso a paso:\n\n1.  **Lee la pregunta:** El gráfico pregunta a 40 estudiantes cuántos eligieron \"Pájaros\".\n2.  **Observa el gráfico:** El gráfico es un diagrama de sectores. El porcentaje de estudiantes que eligieron \"Pájaros\" es el que está en la sección amarilla.\n3.  **Encuentra el porcentaje:** El gráfico muestra que el porcentaje de \"Pájaros\" es 10%.\n4.  **Calcula el número de estudiantes:** Para encontrar cuántos estudiantes eligieron \"Pájaros\", multiplicamos el porcentaje por el número total de estudiantes:\n    - 10% de 40 = (10/100) × 40 = 0.10 × 40 = 4\n\nPor lo tanto, 4 estudiantes eligieron \"Pájaros\".\n\n**Respuesta final:** $\\boxed{4}$"}
{"id": "eval-000224", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "numberline", "answer": "-10", "pred": "-10", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "The red point is located at the number -10 on the number line.\n\nThe final answer is: $\\boxed{-10}$"}
{"id": "eval-000225", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "slope", "answer": "-3/4", "pred": "-\\frac{3}{4}", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, aquí tienes la solución paso a paso:\n\nLa pendiente de una recta se calcula usando la fórmula:\n\n$$\nm = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}\n$$\n\nDonde $(x_1, y_1)$ y $(x_2, y_2)$ son las coordenadas de los dos puntos.\n\nEn este caso, los puntos son:\n- $(-1, -3)$\n- $(3, -6)$\n\nAsignamos:\n- $x_1 = -1$, $y_1 = -3$\n- $x_2 = 3$, $y_2 = -6$\n\nAhora, sustituimos en la fórmula:\n\n$$\nm = \\frac{-6 - (-3)}{3 - (-1)} = \\frac{-6 + 3}{3 + 1} = \\frac{-3}{4}\n$$\n\nEntonces, la pendiente es:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{-\\frac{3}{4}}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000226", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pie", "answer": "10", "pred": "10", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find how many students chose Pears, follow these steps:\n\n1.  The pie chart shows the percentage of students who chose each fruit.\n2.  The percentage for Pears is 25%.\n3.  The total number of students is 40.\n4.  To find the number of students who chose Pears, multiply the total number of students by the percentage for Pears:\n    $40 \\times \\frac{25}{100} = 40 \\times 0.25 = 10$\n\nSo, 10 students chose Pears.\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{10}$"}
{"id": "eval-000227", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "counting", "answer": "11", "pred": null, "correct": false, "boxed": false, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Of course! Let's break down the image step by step.\n\nThe question asks for the total number of shapes that are either stars or squares.\n\n1.  **Identify the shapes:**\n    -   **Stars:** These are the five-pointed stars in the image.\n    -   **Squares:** These are the four-sided squares.\n\n2.  **Count the stars:**\n    -   There is 1 red star.\n    -   There is 1 yellow star.\n    -   There is 1 green star.\n    -   There is 1 orange star.\n    -   There is 1 yellow star.\n    -   There is 1 red star.\n    -   There is 1 green star.\n    -   There is 1 yellow star.\n    -   There is 1 red star.\n    -   There is 1 orange star.\n    -   There is 1 green star.\n    -   There is 1 yellow star.\n    -   There is 1 red star.\n    -   There is 1 green star.\n    -   There is 1 yellow star.\n    -   There is 1 red star.\n    -   There is 1 green star.\n    -   There is 1 yellow star.\n    -   There is 1 red star.\n    -   There is 1 green star.\n    -   There is 1 yellow star.\n    -   There is 1 red star.\n    -   There is 1 green star.\n    -   There is 1 yellow star.\n    -   There is 1 red star.\n    -   There is 1 green star.\n    -   There is 1 yellow star.\n    -   There is 1 red star.\n    -   There is 1 green star.\n    -   There is 1 yellow star.\n    -   There is 1 red star.\n    -   There is 1 green star.\n    -   There is 1 yellow star.\n    -   There is 1 red star.\n    -   There is 1 green star.\n    -   There is 1 yellow star.\n    -   There is 1 red star.\n    -   There is 1 green star.\n    -   There is 1 yellow star.\n    -   There is 1 red star.\n    -   There is 1 green star.\n    -   There is 1 yellow star.\n    -   There is 1 red star.\n    -  "}
{"id": "eval-000228", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "triangle", "answer": "62", "pred": "62^\\circ", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para hallar el valor del ángulo \\( x \\) en el triángulo, usamos la propiedad de que la suma de los ángulos internos de un triángulo es \\( 180^\\circ \\).\n\nLos ángulos dados son:\n- \\( 62^\\circ \\)\n- \\( 56^\\circ \\)\n- \\( x \\)\n\nSumamos los dos ángulos conocidos:\n\\[\n62^\\circ + 56^\\circ = 118^\\circ\n\\]\n\nEntonces, para encontrar \\( x \\):\n\\[\nx = 180^\\circ - 118^\\circ = 62^\\circ\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{62^\\circ}\n\\]"}
{"id": "eval-000229", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "barchart", "answer": "10", "pred": "10", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find how many more votes Monday has than Thursday, we need to:\n\n1. Find the number of votes for Monday from the bar chart. The bar for Monday is at 30 on the y-axis. So, Monday has 30 votes.\n2. Find the number of votes for Thursday. The bar for Thursday is at 20 on the y-axis. So, Thursday has 20 votes.\n3. Subtract the number of votes for Thursday from the number of votes for Monday: 30 - 20 = 10.\n\nTherefore, Monday has 10 more votes than Thursday.\n\n\\boxed{10}"}
{"id": "eval-000230", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "barchart", "answer": "50", "pred": "50", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para encontrar los votos de las manzanas, miramos la barra correspondiente a \"Manzanas\" en la gráfica.\n\nLa barra de \"Manzanas\" llega a la línea que representa 50 en el eje vertical.\n\nPor lo tanto, los votos de las manzanas son 50.\n\n\\boxed{50}"}
{"id": "eval-000231", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pythagoras", "answer": "25", "pred": "25", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "The triangle is a right triangle, so we can use the Pythagorean theorem: $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$, where $a$ and $b$ are the legs and $c$ is the hypotenuse.\n\nGiven:\n- One leg = 20\n- Other leg = 15\n- Hypotenuse = $x$\n\nSo:\n$$\n20^2 + 15^2 = x^2\n$$\n$$\n400 + 225 = x^2\n$$\n$$\nx^2 = 625\n$$\n$$\nx = \\sqrt{625} = 25\n$$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{25}$"}
{"id": "eval-000232", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "rectangle", "answer": "27", "pred": "27 \\, \\text{cm}^2", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, con gusto. Para calcular el área de un rectángulo, usamos la fórmula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Área} = \\text{Base} \\times \\text{Altura}\n$$\n\nEn este caso, la base es 3 cm y la altura es 9 cm.\n\n$$\n\\text{Área} = 3 \\, \\text{cm} \\times 9 \\, \\text{cm} = 27 \\, \\text{cm}^2\n$$\n\nLa respuesta es: $\\boxed{27 \\, \\text{cm}^2}$."}
{"id": "eval-000233", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "equation", "answer": "4", "pred": "4", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, aquí tienes el paso a paso para resolver la ecuación:\n\nLa ecuación es:\n$$7x - 14 = 14$$\n\n**Paso 1:** Suma 14 a ambos lados de la ecuación para aislar el término con $x$.\n$$7x - 14 + 14 = 14 + 14$$\n$$7x = 28$$\n\n**Paso 2:** Divide ambos lados por 7 para hallar el valor de $x$.\n$$\\frac{7x}{7} = \\frac{28}{7}$$\n$$x = 4$$\n\nLa solución es: $\\boxed{4}$"}
{"id": "eval-000234", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "prices", "answer": "5.00", "pred": "5.00", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Of course! Let's break it down step by step.\n\n1.  **Find the total cost of the items Emma bought.**\n    - She bought 2 erasers. Each eraser costs $2.50.\n    - So, the cost of the erasers is: $2 \\times 2.50 = 5.00$\n    - She also bought 4 sandwiches. Each sandwich costs $2.50.\n    - So, the cost of the sandwiches is: $4 \\times 2.50 = 10.00$\n    - Now, add the cost of the erasers and sandwiches together: $5.00 + 10.00 = 15.00$\n\n2.  **Calculate the change.**\n    - Emma paid with a $20 bill.\n    - Change = Amount paid - Total cost\n    - Change = $20.00 - 15.00 = 5.00$\n\nSo, Emma gets $5.00 in change.\n\n$\\boxed{5.00}$"}
{"id": "eval-000235", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "equation", "answer": "4", "pred": "4", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "¡Claro! Vamos a resolver la ecuación paso a paso:\n\nLa ecuación es:\n$$\n3x - 6 = 7x - 22\n$$\n\n**Paso 1:** Restar $7x$ de ambos lados para aislar los términos con $x$ en un lado.\n\n$$\n3x - 6 - 7x = -22\n$$\n\nSimplificamos:\n$$\n-4x - 6 = -22\n$$\n\n**Paso 2:** Sumar 6 a ambos lados para despejar el término con $x$.\n\n$$\n-4x = -22 + 6\n$$\n$$\n-4x = -16\n$$\n\n**Paso 3:** Dividir ambos lados por -4 para hallar el valor de $x$.\n\n$$\nx = \\frac{-16}{-4}\n$$\n$$\nx = 4\n$$\n\n✅ La solución es: $x = 4$\n\n\\boxed{4}"}
{"id": "eval-000236", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "circle", "answer": "4\\pi", "pred": "4\\pi", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the circumference of a circle, use the formula:\n\n$$\nC = 2\\pi r\n$$\n\nGiven that the radius $ r = 2 $ meters, substitute this value into the formula:\n\n$$\nC = 2\\pi \\times 2 = 4\\pi\n$$\n\nSo, the circumference is $ 4\\pi $ meters.\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{4\\pi}$"}
{"id": "eval-000237", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "prices", "answer": "18.50", "pred": "18.50", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, vamos a resolver esto paso a paso.\n\n1. Primero, encontramos el precio de cada artículo en la tabla:\n   - Sándwich: $4.00\n   - Cuaderno: $1.25\n   - Regla: $2.00\n   - Jugo: $3.00\n\n2. Luis compra 4 sándwiches, así que multiplicamos el precio del sándwich por 4:\n   - $4.00 × 4 = $16.00\n\n3. Luis compra 2 cuadernos, así que multiplicamos el precio del cuaderno por 2:\n   - $1.25 × 2 = $2.50\n\n4. Ahora, sumamos los dos montos:\n   - $16.00 + $2.50 = $18.50\n\nEntonces, Luis paga un total de $18.50.\n\n\\boxed{18.50}"}
{"id": "eval-000238", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "equation", "answer": "-6", "pred": "-6", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To solve the equation, follow these steps:\n\n1.  **Move all the x terms to one side and the constants to the other.**  \n    Subtract $4x$ from both sides:  \n    $7x - 4x - 2 = -20$  \n    Simplify:  \n    $3x - 2 = -20$\n\n2.  **Move the constant to the other side.**  \n    Add 2 to both sides:  \n    $3x = -20 + 2$  \n    $3x = -18$\n\n3.  **Solve for x.**  \n    Divide both sides by 3:  \n    $x = -18 / 3$  \n    $x = -6$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{-6}$"}
{"id": "eval-000239", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "barchart", "answer": "4", "pred": "4", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find how many more votes Rabbits have than Fish, we need to:\n\n1. Find the number of votes for Rabbits from the bar chart. The bar for Rabbits is at 8.\n2. Find the number of votes for Fish from the bar chart. The bar for Fish is at 4.\n3. Subtract the number of votes for Fish from the number of votes for Rabbits: 8 - 4 = 4.\n\nSo, Rabbits have 4 more votes than Fish.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{4}"}
{"id": "eval-000240", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "circle", "answer": "50\\pi", "pred": "50\\pi", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the circumference of a circle, use the formula:\n\n$$\nC = \\pi \\times d\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the diameter.\n\nGiven: $d = 50$ m\n\n$$\nC = \\pi \\times 50 = 50\\pi \\text{ m}\n$$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{50\\pi}$ m"}
{"id": "eval-000241", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "triangle", "answer": "93", "pred": "93^\\circ", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para hallar el valor del ángulo $ x $, usamos la suma de los ángulos internos de un triángulo, que siempre es $ 180^\\circ $.\n\nDado:\n- Un ángulo es $ 30^\\circ $\n- Otro ángulo es $ 57^\\circ $\n- El tercer ángulo es $ x $\n\nEntonces:\n$$\nx = 180^\\circ - 30^\\circ - 57^\\circ\n$$\n$$\nx = 180^\\circ - 87^\\circ\n$$\n$$\nx = 93^\\circ\n$$\n\nFinalmente:\n$$\n\\boxed{93^\\circ}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000242", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pie", "answer": "6", "pred": "6", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find how many students chose Mangoes, follow these steps:\n\n1.  The pie chart shows the percentage of students who chose each fruit.\n2.  The percentage for Mangoes is 15%.\n3.  We need to find 15% of 40 students.\n\nCalculate:\n$ 15\\% \\times 40 = \\frac{15}{100} \\times 40 = 0.15 \\times 40 = 6 $\n\nSo, 6 students chose Mangoes.\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{6}$"}
{"id": "eval-000243", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "equation", "answer": "-9", "pred": "-9", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "¡Claro! Vamos a resolver la ecuación paso a paso.\n\nLa ecuación es:\n$$6x + 14 = -40$$\n\n**Paso 1: Restar 14 de ambos lados.**  \nQueremos aislar el término con $x$. Para hacerlo, restamos 14 de ambos lados de la ecuación:\n\n$$6x + 14 - 14 = -40 - 14$$\n$$6x = -54$$\n\n**Paso 2: Dividir ambos lados por 6.**  \nAhora, para despejar $x$, dividimos ambos lados por 6:\n\n$$\\frac{6x}{6} = \\frac{-54}{6}$$\n$$x = -9$$\n\n**Respuesta final:**\n$$\\boxed{-9}$$"}
{"id": "eval-000244", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "cuboid", "answer": "231", "pred": "231", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the volume of a box, we use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Volume} = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width} \\times \\text{height}\n$$\n\nFrom the image:\n- Length = 11 m\n- Width = 7 m\n- Height = 3 m\n\nNow plug in the values:\n\n$$\n\\text{Volume} = 11 \\times 7 \\times 3 = 231 \\text{ m}^3\n$$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{231}$ m³"}
{"id": "eval-000245", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "rectangle", "answer": "36", "pred": "36", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para encontrar el perímetro de un rectángulo, usamos la fórmula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Perímetro} = 2 \\times (\\text{ancho} + \\text{altura})\n$$\n\nEn este caso:\n- Ancho = 15 cm\n- Altura = 3 cm\n\nSustituyendo:\n\n$$\n\\text{Perímetro} = 2 \\times (15 + 3) = 2 \\times 18 = 36 \\text{ cm}\n$$\n\nFinalmente:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{36} \\text{ cm}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000246", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "triangle", "answer": "74", "pred": "74^\\circ", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, veamos paso a paso cómo resolver este problema.\n\nEl triángulo tiene tres ángulos: 69°, 37° y el ángulo que buscamos, x.\n\nEn todo triángulo, la suma de los tres ángulos es siempre 180°.\n\nEntonces, podemos escribir la ecuación:\n69° + 37° + x = 180°\n\nAhora, sumamos los dos ángulos que conocemos:\n69 + 37 = 106\n\nEntonces:\n106 + x = 180\n\nPara encontrar x, restamos 106 de 180:\n180 - 106 = 74\n\nPor lo tanto, el valor de x es 74°.\n\n\\boxed{74^\\circ}"}
{"id": "eval-000247", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "prices", "answer": "2.50", "pred": "2.50", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, vamos paso a paso:\n\n1. **Calcular el precio total de los cuadernos:**\n   - Liam compra 6 cuadernos, cada uno por $0.50.\n   - $ 6 \\times 0.50 = 3.00 $ dólares.\n\n2. **Calcular el precio total de las manzanas:**\n   - Liam compra 3 manzanas, cada una por $1.50.\n   - $ 3 \\times 1.50 = 4.50 $ dólares.\n\n3. **Sumar los costos totales:**\n   - $ 3.00 + 4.50 = 7.50 $ dólares.\n\n4. **Restar el total pagado de la cantidad que le dieron:**\n   - Liam paga con un billete de $10.\n   - $ 10 - 7.50 = 2.50 $ dólares.\n\n**Respuesta final:** $\\boxed{2.50}$"}
{"id": "eval-000248", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "cuboid", "answer": "124", "pred": "124", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the total surface area of a box, we need to calculate the sum of the areas of all six faces.\n\nThe box is a rectangular prism, so it has:\n- Two pairs of identical faces: front/back, left/right, top/bottom.\n\nThe dimensions given are:\n- Length = 9 cm\n- Width = 4 cm\n- Height = 2 cm\n\nThe formula for the total surface area of a rectangular prism is:\n$$\n\\text{Surface Area} = 2(lw + lh + wh)\n$$\nwhere:\n- $l$ = length\n- $w$ = width\n- $h$ = height\n\nSubstitute the values:\n$$\n\\text{Surface Area} = 2(9 \\times 4 + 9 \\times 2 + 4 \\times 2)\n$$\n\nCalculate each product:\n- $9 \\times 4 = 36$\n- $9 \\times 2 = 18$\n- $4 \\times 2 = 8$\n\nAdd them: $36 + 18 + 8 = 62$\n\nNow multiply by 2: $2 \\times 62 = 124$\n\nSo, the total surface area is 124 cm².\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{124}$ cm²"}
{"id": "eval-000249", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "equation", "answer": "4", "pred": "4", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To solve the equation $3x + 9 = 21$, follow these steps:\n\n1. Subtract 9 from both sides to isolate the term with $x$:\n   $$\n   3x = 21 - 9\n   $$\n   $$\n   3x = 12\n   $$\n\n2. Divide both sides by 3:\n   $$\n   x = \\frac{12}{3}\n   $$\n   $$\n   x = 4\n   $$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{4}$"}
{"id": "eval-000250", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pie", "answer": "18", "pred": "18", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Of course! Let's break it down step by step.\n\nThe pie chart shows the results of a survey with 120 students. We need to find out how many students chose Tuesday.\n\n1.  **Find the percentage for Tuesday:** Look at the chart. The blue slice represents Tuesday, and it is labeled with **15%**.\n\n2.  **Convert the percentage to a number:** We need to find out how many students chose Tuesday. We can do this by multiplying the percentage by the total number of students.\n\n    $$\n    15\\% \\times 120 = \\frac{15}{100} \\times 120 = 0.15 \\times 120 = 18\n    $$\n\nSo, 18 students chose Tuesday.\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer:** $\\boxed{18}$"}
