{"id": "eval-000252", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "circle", "answer": "64\\pi", "pred": "64\\pi", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Of course! To find the area of a circle, we use the formula:\n\n$$\nA = \\pi r^2\n$$\n\nHere, the radius $ r $ is given as 8 mm. So, we substitute $ r = 8 $ into the formula:\n\n$$\nA = \\pi (8)^2 = \\pi \\times 64\n$$\n\nSo, the area of the circle is:\n\n$$\n64\\pi \\text{ mm}^2\n$$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{64\\pi}$"}
{"id": "eval-000253", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "circle", "answer": "12\\pi", "pred": "12\\pi", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para hallar la longitud de la circunferencia, usamos la fórmula:\n\n\\[\nC = \\pi \\times d\n\\]\n\nDonde \\( d \\) es el diámetro. En este caso, el diámetro es 12 mm.\n\n\\[\nC = \\pi \\times 12 = 12\\pi \\text{ mm}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{12\\pi}\n\\]"}
{"id": "eval-000254", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "rectangle", "answer": "30", "pred": "30 \\, \\text{m}^2", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the area of a rectangle, use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area} = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width}\n$$\n\nFrom the image:\n- Length = 10 m\n- Width = 3 m\n\nNow plug in the values:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area} = 10 \\, \\text{m} \\times 3 \\, \\text{m} = 30 \\, \\text{m}^2\n$$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{30 \\, \\text{m}^2}$"}
{"id": "eval-000255", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "pythagoras", "answer": "26", "pred": "2\\sqrt{29}", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "El triángulo es rectángulo, por lo que podemos usar el teorema de Pitágoras. En un triángulo rectángulo, el cuadrado de la hipotenusa (la lado más largo) es igual a la suma de los cuadrados de los otros dos lados.\n\nLos lados dados son:\n- Lado vertical: 4 m\n- Lado horizontal: 10 m\n- Hipotenusa: x\n\nAplicando el teorema de Pitágoras:\n$$\nx^2 = 4^2 + 10^2\n$$\n$$\nx^2 = 16 + 100\n$$\n$$\nx^2 = 116\n$$\n$$\nx = \\sqrt{116}\n$$\n$$\nx = \\sqrt{4 \\times 29} = 2\\sqrt{29}\n$$\n\nEntonces, el valor de $x$ es $2\\sqrt{29}$ metros.\n\nFinalmente, la respuesta es:\n$$\n\\boxed{2\\sqrt{29}}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000256", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "circle", "answer": "48\\pi", "pred": "48\\pi", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para hallar la longitud de la circunferencia, usamos la fórmula:\n\n$$\nC = \\pi \\cdot d\n$$\n\nDonde $d$ es el diámetro. En este caso, el diámetro es $48$ m.\n\nSustituyendo:\n\n$$\nC = \\pi \\cdot 48 = 48\\pi \\text{ m}\n$$\n\nFinalmente:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{48\\pi} \\text{ m}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000257", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "fraction", "answer": "3/4", "pred": "\\frac{3}{4}", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "The circle is divided into 4 equal parts. 3 of the 4 parts are shaded. So, the fraction of the shape that is shaded is 3/4. This is already in simplest form.\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{\\frac{3}{4}}$"}
{"id": "eval-000258", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "rectangle", "answer": "40", "pred": "40", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para encontrar el perímetro de un rectángulo, usamos la fórmula:\n\n$$\nP = 2 \\times (ancho + altura)\n$$\n\nEn este caso:\n- Ancho = 14 m\n- Altura = 6 m\n\nSustituyendo:\n\n$$\nP = 2 \\times (14 + 6) = 2 \\times 20 = 40 \\text{ m}\n$$\n\nFinalmente:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{40} \\text{ m}\n$$"}
{"id": "eval-000259", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "column_op", "answer": "2112", "pred": "2112", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para resolver la operación, multiplicamos 264 por 8.\n\nPrimero, multiplicamos las unidades:  \n8 × 4 = 32.  \nEscribimos 2 y llevamos 3.\n\nLuego, multiplicamos las decenas:  \n8 × 6 = 48.  \nSumamos el 3 que llevamos: 48 + 3 = 51.  \nEscribimos 1 y llevamos 5.\n\nFinalmente, multiplicamos las centenas:  \n8 × 2 = 16.  \nSumamos el 5 que llevamos: 16 + 5 = 21.  \nEscribimos 21.\n\nEntonces, 264 × 8 = 2112.\n\n\\boxed{2112}"}
{"id": "eval-000260", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "equation", "answer": "-3", "pred": "-3", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para resolver la ecuación, primero se debe aislar la variable x. Se hace esto eliminando los términos constantes.\n\n1.  Restar 7 de ambos lados de la ecuación:\n    $5x + 7 = -8$\n    $5x + 7 - 7 = -8 - 7$\n    $5x = -15$\n\n2.  Dividir ambos lados por 5:\n    $5x = -15$\n    $x = -15 / 5$\n    $x = -3$\n\nLa solución es $x = -3$.\n\n\\boxed{-3}"}
{"id": "eval-000261", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "equation", "answer": "-9", "pred": "-9", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, vamos a resolver la ecuación paso a paso.\n\nLa ecuación es:\n$$2(x - 2) = -22$$\n\n**Paso 1: Expande el lado izquierdo.**\nUsamos la distributiva (el \"distributivo\" de los paréntesis):\n$$2 \\cdot x - 2 \\cdot 2 = -22$$\n$$2x - 4 = -22$$\n\n**Paso 2: Suma 4 a ambos lados.**\nPara aislar el término con $x$, sumamos 4 a ambos lados:\n$$2x - 4 + 4 = -22 + 4$$\n$$2x = -18$$\n\n**Paso 3: Divide ambos lados por 2.**\nDividimos ambos lados por 2 para hallar el valor de $x$:\n$$x = \\frac{-18}{2}$$\n$$x = -9$$\n\n**Respuesta final:**\n$$\\boxed{-9}$$"}
{"id": "eval-000262", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "prices", "answer": "7.00", "pred": "7.00", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the total amount Valeria pays, we need to calculate the cost of the juices and the pencils she buys.\n\n1.  **Find the cost of the juices:**  \n    Valeria buys 4 juices, and each juice costs $0.25.  \n    Total cost for juices = 4 × $0.25 = $1.00\n\n2.  **Find the cost of the pencils:**  \n    Valeria buys 4 pencils, and each pencil costs $1.50.  \n    Total cost for pencils = 4 × $1.50 = $6.00\n\n3.  **Add the costs together:**  \n    Total cost = $1.00 (juices) + $6.00 (pencils) = $7.00\n\nSo, Valeria pays a total of $7.00.\n\n\\boxed{7.00}"}
{"id": "eval-000263", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "fraction", "answer": "1/12", "pred": "\\frac{1}{10}", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the fraction of the shape that is shaded, we need to count the shaded parts and the total number of parts.\n\n- The shape is a rectangle divided into 10 equal vertical bars.\n- There is 1 shaded bar.\n\nSo, the fraction is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{10}\n$$\n\nThis fraction is already in its simplest form.\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{\\frac{1}{10}}$"}
{"id": "eval-000264", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "circle", "answer": "24\\pi", "pred": "24\\pi", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the circumference of a circle, use the formula:\n\n$$\nC = \\pi \\times d\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the diameter.\n\nGiven: $d = 24$ cm\n\n$$\nC = \\pi \\times 24 = 24\\pi \\text{ cm}\n$$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{24\\pi}$ cm"}
{"id": "eval-000265", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "fraction", "answer": "3/4", "pred": "\\frac{2}{3}", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "La figura tiene 12 partes iguales. El número de partes coloreadas es 8.\n\nLa fracción es: 8/12.\n\nSimplificamos: 8/12 = 2/3.\n\nLa fracción de la figura que está coloreada es: \\boxed{\\frac{2}{3}}."}
{"id": "eval-000266", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "counting", "answer": "4", "pred": "5", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Let's count the triangles and the stars in the image.\n\n- **Triangles**:  \n  - Red triangle: 1  \n  - Blue triangle: 1  \n  - Yellow triangle: 1  \n  - Blue triangle: 1  \n  - Yellow triangle: 1  \n  - Orange triangle: 1  \n  - Yellow triangle: 1  \n  - Total triangles: 7\n\n- **Stars**:  \n  - Blue star: 1  \n  - Yellow star: 1  \n  - Total stars: 2\n\nNow, subtract the number of stars from the number of triangles:  \n$7 - 2 = 5$\n\nThere are 5 more triangles than stars.\n\n$\\boxed{5}$"}
{"id": "eval-000267", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "column_op", "answer": "21201", "pred": "21189", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Para resolver la multiplicación:  \n573 × 37\n\nPrimero, descomponer 37 en 30 + 7.\n\nEntonces:  \n573 × 37 = 573 × (30 + 7) = 573 × 30 + 573 × 7\n\nCalculamos cada parte:\n\n- 573 × 30 = 573 × 3 × 10 = 1719 × 10 = 17,190\n- 573 × 7 = 573 × 5 + 573 × 2 = 2,865 + 1,146 = 3,999\n\nSumamos:  \n17,190 + 3,999 = 21,189\n\nFinalmente:  \n573 × 37 = 21,189\n\n\\boxed{21189}"}
{"id": "eval-000268", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": "fraction", "answer": "3/4", "pred": "\\frac{7}{10}", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Of course! Let's break it down step by step.\n\n1.  **Count the total number of parts:** Look at the shape. It's a long rectangle divided into 10 equal vertical sections. So, the total number of parts is 10.\n\n2.  **Count the shaded parts:** Now, count how many of these sections are shaded. There are 7 shaded sections.\n\n3.  **Write the fraction:** The fraction of the shape that is shaded is the number of shaded parts divided by the total number of parts. So, it's $\\frac{7}{10}$.\n\n4.  **Simplify the fraction:** Is this fraction in its simplest form? We check if the numerator (7) and the denominator (10) have any common factors other than 1. Since 7 is a prime number and doesn't divide 10, the fraction $\\frac{7}{10}$ is already in simplest form.\n\nSo, the final answer is $\\boxed{\\frac{7}{10}}$."}
{"id": "eval-000269", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "prices", "answer": "5.00", "pred": "5.00", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, vamos paso a paso:\n\n1. **Encuentra el precio de las manzanas:**  \n   Mateo compra 2 manzanas, y cada manzana cuesta $1.50.  \n   $ 2 \\times 1.50 = 3.00 $  \n   → Paga $3.00 por las manzanas.\n\n2. **Encuentra el precio de los cuadernos:**  \n   Mateo compra 4 cuadernos, y cada cuaderno cuesta $0.50.  \n   $ 4 \\times 0.50 = 2.00 $  \n   → Paga $2.00 por los cuadernos.\n\n3. **Suma el total de lo que paga:**  \n   $ 3.00 + 2.00 = 5.00 $  \n   → Mateo paga un total de $5.00.\n\n4. **Resta el total de lo que paga de lo que paga con el billete:**  \n   Mateo paga con un billete de $10.  \n   $ 10.00 - 5.00 = 5.00 $  \n   → Le devuelven $5.00.\n\n**Final:** $\\boxed{5.00}$"}
{"id": "eval-000270", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "circle", "answer": "18\\pi", "pred": "18\\pi", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the circumference of a circle, use the formula:\n\n$$\nC = \\pi \\times d\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the diameter.\n\nGiven: $d = 18$ mm\n\n$$\nC = \\pi \\times 18 = 18\\pi \\text{ mm}\n$$\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{18\\pi}$ mm"}
{"id": "eval-000271", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "equation", "answer": "3", "pred": null, "correct": false, "boxed": false, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To solve the equation, follow these steps:\n\n1.  **Isolate the variable**: Add 6 to both sides of the equation to get rid of the -6 on the left.\n    - $5x - 6 + 6 = 9 + 6$\n    - $5x = 15$\n\n2.  **Solve for x**: Divide both sides by 5.\n    - $\\frac{5x}{5} = \\frac{15}{5}$\n    - $x = 3$\n\nThe solution is $x = 3$."}
{"id": "eval-000272", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "numberline", "answer": "1.5", "pred": "1.4", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To solve this, we need to determine the number that the red point marks on the number line.\n\n1. Look at the number line. The number 0 is at the left end.\n2. The number 1.75 is at the right end.\n3. The red point is located between 0 and 1.75.\n4. The number line is divided into 10 equal parts between 0 and 1.75. This means each part is 0.175 (or 1/10) units.\n5. The red point is at the 8th mark from 0. So, the number is 0 + 8 × 0.175 = 1.4.\n\nTherefore, the red point marks the number 1.4.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{1.4}"}
{"id": "eval-000273", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "primaria", "family": "prices", "answer": "30.00", "pred": "30.00", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Claro, vamos paso a paso:\n\n1. Primero, calculamos el precio total de los lápices.  \n   Sofía compra 4 lápices, cada uno cuesta $2.00.  \n   $ 4 \\times 2.00 = 8.00 $ dólares.\n\n2. Luego, calculamos el precio total de los jugos.  \n   Sofía compra 4 jugos, cada uno cuesta $3.00.  \n   $ 4 \\times 3.00 = 12.00 $ dólares.\n\n3. Ahora, sumamos los costos totales:  \n   $ 8.00 + 12.00 = 20.00 $ dólares.\n\n4. Sofía paga con un billete de $50.  \n   El cambio que le devuelven es:  \n   $ 50.00 - 20.00 = 30.00 $ dólares.\n\n**Respuesta final:** $\\boxed{30.00}$"}
{"id": "eval-000274", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "slope", "answer": "3", "pred": "3", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "To find the slope of the line through the two points (1, -4) and (3, 2), use the slope formula:\n\n$$\nm = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates:\n- $ (x_1, y_1) = (1, -4) $\n- $ (x_2, y_2) = (3, 2) $\n\n$$\nm = \\frac{2 - (-4)}{3 - 1} = \\frac{2 + 4}{2} = \\frac{6}{2} = 3\n$$\n\nThe slope of the line is 3.\n\n\\boxed{3}"}
{"id": "eval-000275", "source": "synth", "lang": "en", "band": "secundaria", "family": "sequence", "answer": "21875", "pred": "21875", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Let's analyze the sequence: 7, 35, 175, 875, 4375, ?\n\nFirst, look at the pattern between the numbers:\n\n- 7 to 35: 35 = 7 × 5\n- 35 to 175: 175 = 35 × 5\n- 175 to 875: 875 = 175 × 5\n- 875 to 4375: 4375 = 875 × 5\n\nSo, each term is the previous term multiplied by 5.\n\nLet's verify:\n- 7 × 5 = 35 ✓\n- 35 × 5 = 175 ✓\n- 175 × 5 = 875 ✓\n- 875 × 5 = 4375 ✓\n\nSo the pattern is: each term is the previous term × 5.\n\nTherefore, the next term is:\n4375 × 5 = 21,875\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{21875}"}
{"id": "eval-000276", "source": "synth", "lang": "es", "band": "secundaria", "family": "triangle", "answer": "28", "pred": "8^\\circ", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "¡Claro! Vamos a resolver esto paso a paso.\n\nEl triángulo es un triángulo rectángulo, lo que significa que uno de sus ángulos es 90°. Los ángulos en un triángulo suman 180°.\n\nSabemos que:\n- Un ángulo es 90°.\n- Otro ángulo es 82°.\n- El tercer ángulo es \\( x \\).\n\nUsamos la fórmula:\n\\[\n90^\\circ + 82^\\circ + x = 180^\\circ\n\\]\n\nSumamos los dos ángulos conocidos:\n\\[\n172^\\circ + x = 180^\\circ\n\\]\n\nRestamos 172° de ambos lados:\n\\[\nx = 180^\\circ - 172^\\circ = 8^\\circ\n\\]\n\nEntonces, el valor de \\( x \\) es \\( 8^\\circ \\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{8^\\circ}\n\\]"}
