l volume} = 32\n$$\n\nThen:\n\n$$\n\\text{Original volume} = 2 \\times 32 = 64 \\text{ ounces}\n$$\n\nSo, the original volume of tomatoes was 64 ounces.\n\nNow, each"}
{"id": "mgsm-en-098", "source": "mgsm_en", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": null, "answer": "5", "pred": "25", "correct": false, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Of course! Let's solve this step by step.\n\nThe problem says:\n- There were originally 30 cars on the motorway.\n- Then, 5 cars left the line to take an exit.\n- The cars that were still in line drove through the jam.\n\nSo, the number of cars that drove through the jam is the original number minus the cars that left.\n\nLet's do the math:\n- Original number of cars: 30\n- Cars that left: 5\n- Cars that drove through the jam: 30 - 5 = 25\n\nSo, 25 cars drove through the jam in the first 15 minutes.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{25}$."}
{"id": "mgsm-en-099", "source": "mgsm_en", "lang": "en", "band": "primaria", "family": null, "answer": "58", "pred": "58", "correct": true, "boxed": true, "lang_ok": true, "reply": "Sure! Let's break it down step by step.\n\n1. **Find out how many potted plants Mary already has:**\n   - She has 2 potted plants on each of 40 window ledges.\n   - So, total plants = 2 plants/ledge × 40 ledges = 80 plants.\n\n2. **Add the new plants she received:**\n   - She received 18 new potted plants.\n   - So, total plants now = 80 + 18 = 98 plants.\n\n3. **Calculate how many plants she gives away:**\n   - She gives 1 potted plant from each of the 40 ledges.\n   - So, she gives away 40 plants.\n\n4. **Find out how many plants she has left:**\n   - 98 total plants - 40 given away = 58 plants.\n\nSo, Mary will have 58 potted plants left.\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{58}$"}
